Description: SSC sensor stack for the OnePlus Pad 3 (erhai)
 Brings the ADSP SSC sensors (BMI3x0 accelerometer, ambient light) up to
 iio-sensor-proxy and the GNOME desktop:
  - patched iio-sensor-proxy 3.9 with SSC support + startup-claim-race fix
    (/usr/local/libexec/iio-sensor-proxy), monitor-sensor and ssccli helpers
  - libssc 0.4.4 (/usr/local/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/libssc.so.2)
  - hexagonrpcd 0.4.0 with odm-sensor-config + nonfatal-dispatch patches
    (/usr/local/bin/hexagonrpcd-erhai), a hexagonrpcd.service drop-in that
    points at it, and the complete /var/lib/hexagonfs-erhai remotefs tree
    (acdb, fastrpc_shell_0 + libsns_* DSP libs, vendor sensor configs,
    odm json_list). The tree must be complete BEFORE hexagonrpcd first
    attaches: the ADSP sensor PD loads its configs exactly once.
  - udev rule 90-erhai-ssc-sensors.rules: SSC sensor types + ACCEL_MOUNT_MATRIX
    (rotated -90 deg so natural landscape classifies as "normal") on
    fastrpc-adsp-secure, SYSTEMD_WANTS=iio-sensor-proxy.service
  - iio-sensor-proxy.service drop-in redirecting ExecStart to the SSC build
  - erhai-sensors@erhai.local GNOME Shell quick-settings extension
    (auto-brightness toggle; auto-rotate toggle with laptop-mode greying and
    suppression of the shell's built-in duplicate rotation toggle)
 The source patches for the binary builds ship under
 /usr/share/doc/oneplus-erhai-sensors/patches/.

Package: oneplus-erhai-video
Version: 0.1
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: TheMojoMan <themojoman@gmx.net>
Depends: libva2
Recommends: oneplus-erhai-linux-7.2 (>= 7.2.0-sm8750-themojoman+b10), firefox | chromium | brave-browser
Filename: ./oneplus-erhai-video_0.1_arm64.deb
Size: 1084708
MD5sum: 8c261a71a071faeef73d2a11d4265bd1
SHA1: de716ea71c0f838689aceed92a6e5439e34d8ce2
SHA256: 4d95fc755523443f9204aa7ba6027c32568280bcdfd31b323d662f0fc4fafd7f
Section: video
Priority: optional
Description: Hardware video decoding for the OnePlus Pad 3 (erhai, SM8750)
 Userspace stack for the Qualcomm Iris hardware video decoder (the Venus
 lineage, "Iris Decoder" V4L2 node, qcom_iris kernel module) of the OnePlus
 Pad 3. Ships the iris-vaapi VA-API driver (iris_drv_video.so) so VA-API
 clients drive /dev/videoN directly, plus all browser integration:
 . - /etc/environment.d/55: LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME=iris (libva cannot autodetect
   the driver on msm platform devices)
 . - /etc/environment.d/56: MOZ_DISABLE_RDD_SANDBOX=1 (Firefox VA-API decode
   runs in the RDD process, whose seccomp sandbox blocks /dev/dma_heap)
 . - /etc/firefox/policies/policies.json: locked VA-API decode prefs
 . - /etc/chromium.d/erhai-hw-video: AcceleratedVideoDecoder feature flag
   (chromium's V4L2VideoDecoder drives the iris node directly, no VA-API)
 . - /etc/brave/policies/managed/erhai-hwvideo.json: HardwareAccelerationMode
 . - udev rule giving the video group access to /dev/dma_heap/system
 Codecs: H.264, HEVC Main/Main10, VP9 Profile 0/2 (no AV1). Chromium
 (xtradeb) decodes H.264/VP9 via V4L2; Firefox and Brave decode H.264/HEVC
 Main (and Main10/VP9 P2 where the firmware exposes P010) via VA-API.
 Requires oneplus-erhai-linux-7.2 >= +b10 (decode-order output property) for
 Firefox/Brave; works out of the box in the full erhai image. After
 installing on a running desktop, log out and back in once.
 .
 The iris-vaapi source tree ships in /usr/src/oneplus-erhai-video/iris-vaapi.

